From 33f54cb3fb58efb7d3c9912a6624d00bff0fec81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guillaume Dumoulin <dev@myrole.fr>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:53:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qtfb: let a client show a widget; give the window bar real
 icons
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds MESSAGE_SET_WIDGET (10): in the update slot of ClientMessage, the
rectangle of the client's framebuffer to show as a widget (w or h <= 0
removes it; a rectangle outside the framebuffer drops the client).
MESSAGE_SET_WINDOW_STATE gains WINDOW_STATE_WIDGET (2): the window
becomes a card showing that rectangle 1:1 under a header with the app's
tile, its name, open and close. The card is dragged by its header and
its position is kept per app in widget-positions.json. Input inside the
card reaches the client in framebuffer pixels; a MESSAGE_UPDATE repaints
only the part of the card it touches. Without a widget, state 2
minimizes.

STATE_CHANGED_REASON_VISIBILITY gains 2 (shown as a widget), and the
new STATE_CHANGED_REASON_CAPABILITIES (2) tells a client in the initial
state packets which extensions the server understands (bit 0 window
state, bit 1 widgets).

The minimized window is a compact pill (tile, name, open, close) and
the window bar uses vector icons (Lucide, ISC) instead of the "_",
"□"/"▭" and "X" glyphs.

xovi/make.sh writes rcc's output to a file before trimming it: with
pipefail, sed quitting early killed rcc with SIGPIPE once the resources
outgrew the pipe buffer.
